                \hyphpar0\par\page\pard\sb200\sl20 \b0\fs20\f0 \hyphpar0\par\pard\sl-240 \b\f1 Kannel Architecture and Design$Revision: 1.20 $\hyphpar0\par\pard\sl260 \b0\f0 by\~Lars Wirzenius\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb260\sl260 \lang1033 This document examines the purpose of a gateway in the Wireless Application Protocol (WAP) architecture. WAP is a technology for implementing services on moible phones using hypertext similar to the World WideWeb (WWW). We examine a particular WAP gateway, called Kannel and will discuss its design and look how well it works.\hyphpar0\par\sect\sectd\plain\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1440\margrsxn1440\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1920\headery0\footery0\pgnlcrm{\headerl\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa430\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {}\par}{\footerl\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa910\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 \chpgn }\par}{\headerr\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa430\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {}\par}{\footerr\pard\sl-240\sb770\sa910\plain\tqc\tx4680\tqr\tx9360 {}\tab {}\tab {\i\fs20 \chpgn }\par}\pard\sb311\s1\sl539 \b\fs41\f1 Table of Contents\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb207\li1440\sl260\fi-480 {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _15 }{\fldrslt \fs20\f0 1. Introduction}}\fs20\f0 \tqr\tldot\tx9360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _15 }{\fldrslt {\field\flddirty{\*\fldinst PAGEREF _15}{\fldrslt 000}}}}\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb48\li1440\sl260\fi-480 {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _31 }{\fldrslt 2. Problems in implementing services for mobile phones}}\tqr\tldot\tx9360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _31 }{\fldrslt {\field\flddirty{\*\fldinst PAGEREF _31}{\fldrslt 000}}}}\keepn\hyphpar0\par\pard\sb48\li1920\sl260\fi-480 {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _35 }{\fldrslt \b0 Technical problems}}\b0 \tqr\tldot\tx9360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _35 }{\fldrslt {\field\flddirty{\*\fldinst PAGEREF _35}{\fldrslt 000}}}}\hyphpar0\par\pard\li1920\sl260\fi-480 {\field{\*\fldinst   HYPERLINK  \\l _51 }{\fld